{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no structural gaps. I did not assess runtime behavior independently.\n\n- **Type and trait:** In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs`, the `language!` macro invocation for `PlainText` carries the `{impl}` reference. It expands to `pub struct PlainText;` with `impl super::OutlineLang for PlainText`. The impl defines `name`, `extensions`, `outline` and `fingerprint_scheme`, with the scheme `\"plain-text-structural-v1\"`. It also defines `search_structure`, whose signature matches `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`.\n- **Cheaply cloneable default:** The struct derives `Clone, Copy, Debug, Default`. It is a zero-sized unit struct, so its default value is cheap to clone and shares its configuration.\n- **No claimed extensions:** `extensions()` returns `$profile.extensions`. For `PlainText` that is `super::plain::PROFILE`, which in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]` sets `extensions: &[]` and `language: None`.\n- **Fallback selection:** `Registry::for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/language.rs` returns `None` when the path has no extension. It also returns `None` when no provider claims the lowercased extension. `OutlineContent::parse_source` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs` then falls back to `Self::parse_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`. `profile_for_path` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/profile.rs` falls back to `plain::PROFILE` the same way. This covers filenames without an extension, and no extension-less path can match a registered provider.\n- **Tests:** The tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs` carry `{test}` references. `bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline` asserts the plain-text name and empty extensions. `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` covers the fallback.",
  "references": "d364693a64f673cea5b31c5d57cc4436a3d085824fd398288e275ce0c804733a",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language",
      "matches": [
